{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting It Right"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Common Ground"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe necessity, duty, advice, or strong disaproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le18ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Wh-clause in Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use wh-words to make questions. If the verb requires a preposition, you have to pay attention to the word order in the question."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Many verbs are followed by prepositions, like <span class=\"italic\">listen to, learn about, depend on,</span> and so on."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at how you can use these verb + prepositions in sentences.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Laura <span class=\"strong\">was sharing</span> a cookie <span class=\"strong\">with</span> her friend Celia.<br/> My friends and I <span class=\"strong\">were preparing for</span> our exam.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to ask questions using these verbs and wh-words, notice how the word order can change.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Q: <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">Whom (or who)</span> was</span> Laura <span class=\"strong\">sharing</span> a cookie <span class=\"underline\">with</span>?  <br/>A: With her friend Celia.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "or you can say"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Q: <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">With whom</span> was</span> Laura <span class=\"strong\">sharing</span> a cookie?<br/> A: With her friend Celia.<br/><br/></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Q: <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">What</span> were</span> you and your friends <span class=\"strong\">preparing <span class=\"underline\">for</span></span>?<br/>  A: Our exam.</span><br/><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "or you can say"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Q: <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">For what </span>were</span> you and your friends <span class=\"strong\">preparing</span>?<br/> A: Our exam.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Many people think that leaving a preposition at the end of a question is not correct, but both structures are possible. It can sound more formal if you put the preposition at the beginning."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking about Past Habits"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "To talk about habits in the past, you can use<span class=\"strong\"> would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>. And to talk about habits in the present you can use <span class=\"strong\">will</span>.<br>   If you want to express annoyance in the present, you can also use<span class=\"strong\"> will</span> and <span class=\"strong\">will not</span>. <br> The <span class=\"strong\">Past Continuous</span> verb tense can also express annoyance, but in the past. This verb tense is also used to talk about temporary actions that happened in the past. <br> Similarly, you can use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect Continuous</span> when you want to talk about repeated actions that happened before another time in the past."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"underline\\\">Present Habits\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"underline\\\"> Past Habits\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">will/ will not</span><br/><br/>  <ul><li>when you want to talk about habits and routines</li></ul>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will</span> always <span class=\\\"strong\\\">buy</span> jeans at the Gap. They fit me well and I like the different styles.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span><br/><br/>  <ul><li>to talk about habits or states that happened frequently in the past <li>these habits or states are different from the present <li>used with action verbs and stative verbs</li></ul>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to visit</span> my grandmother every Sunday.<br/><br/> I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to like</span> watching cartoons on Saturday mornings.</span><br/><br/>   <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> <br/><br/><ul><li>used for past habits only <li>not used for past states <li>only used with action verbs</li></ul>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would visit</span> my grandmother every Sunday.<br/><br/>  I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to like</span> watching cartoons on Saturday mornings. </span> (<span class=\\\"underline\\\">not</span><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I <span style=\\\"text-decoration:line-through;\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">would like</span></span> watching cartoons on Saturday mornings.</span>)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"underline\\\">Expressing Annoyance at a Present Habit \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"underline\\\">Expressing Annoyance at a Past Habit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">will/ will not</span><br/><br/>  <ul><li>shows that you are annoyed with a habit that occurs in the present</li></ul>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will bring</span> her cat over to my house even though she knows I'm allergic.<br/><br/>  My brother <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will not stop</span> using that terrible cologne.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past Continuous</span><br/><br/>  <ul><li>use the past continuous with <span class=\\\"italic\\\">always</span>, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">constantly</span> or <span class=\\\"italic\\\">forever</span> to show that you are annoyed with a past habit</li></ul>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">My boss <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was always calling</span> me by the wrong name. It really made me angry since I had been there for 10 years.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\"><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Temporary Habitual Action\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\"><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Temporary Habitual Action Before Another Time in the Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past Continuous</span><br/><br/>  <ul><li>use with a habit that was temporary in the past</li></ul>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">David went to India for work on a two-month contract. He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was eating</span> Indian food for breakfast, lunch and dinner.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past Perfect Continuous</span><br/><br/>  <ul><li>use with a habitual or repeated action that happened before another time in the past</li></ul>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">My friend <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had been spending</span> 5 hours a day training before the marathon last weekend.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to be a counselor."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I would hear all sorts of people blame themselves for expressing things in the wrong way, or feel guilty about having a certain point of view. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was always telling people that disputes are a natural part of human nature. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "common ground"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "area of agreement between two people or groups"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: By listening to the other person, you can sometimes find  common ground. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear when people are talking about feelings and emotions."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shame"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the feeling that you are responsible for something not being right"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you are like me, you may feel shame after getting into a dispute with a colleague, friend, or even a loved one. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "married "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "united to live together after a wedding ceremony"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm married to a wonderful woman."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "we've had our share"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "get more than the usual of something bad"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We've had our share of arguments. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "point of view"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "opinion"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to analyze the situation from a new angle, because there is a part of reality that your brain had been missing: the other person's point of view. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "desirable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something you want to have"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Anger is not a desirable feeling, but it can be useful one, because it shows that the topic of conversation is important to you and that it may be an urgent matter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a group of 3 people, discuss situations in which two people may be in a dispute."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Select one situation for a role play. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Decide who will be the counsellor and who will be the two people in dispute."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do a role play. The people in dispute explain their point of view. The counsellor tries to help them settle the dispute."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try to use expressions of annoyance in this lesson, such as for Pete's sake or for heaven's sake."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles so that each person acts as counsellor one time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "After the role play, discuss the techniques for settling the dispute that were used in the role play. Are they effective techniques?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss situations leading people to disputes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain my point of view in a dispute."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express annoyance using appropriate expressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give suggestions for settling a dispute."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le18ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le18ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le18ob10re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<p>Good evening, ladies and gentlemen. I know it's getting late, so I'll keep my remarks brief. My name is Hank Josephson. Can you guess what I'm going to talk about? I would like to talk to you about how to resolve interpersonal disputes. If you are like me, you may feel shame after getting into a dispute with a colleague, friend, or even a loved one. I used to be a counselor. I would hear all sorts of people blame themselves for expressing things in the wrong way, or feel guilty about having a certain point of view. I was always telling people that disputes are a natural part of human nature.</p>", "id": 1, "time": "100 ", "image": "engenn10le18ob10re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<p>I'm married to a wonderful woman, but we've had our share of arguments. Anger is not a desirable feeling, but it can be a useful one, because it shows that the topic of conversation is important to you and that it may be an urgent matter.</p>", "id": 2, "time": "41000", "image": "engenn10le18ob10re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<p>First, let's understand anger. Anger can be defined as a temporary loss of power.  I suspect it arises when someone challenges your role or authority to take a course of action. The emotional side of your brain has taken over. Sound familiar? Do you remember what you have to do? It is difficult, but in my view, very important that you kick start your rational brain. You want to say: \u201cI can't believe it!\u201d Or, \u201cwhy does this always happen?\u201d What you need to say is: \u201cLet's talk about this calmly for a minute\u201d. You need to analyze the situation from a new angle, because there is a part of reality that your  brain had been missing: the other person's point of view. By listening to the other person, you can sometimes find a very beautiful thing. Do you know what I am talking about? It's called common ground.</p>", "id": 3, "time": "58000", "image": "engenn10le18ob10re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about beliefs, opinion, and express annoyance."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report details, reasons, or results of events or actions.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about past habits.  "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you think it is possible to avoid disputes between people? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What situations are more likely to lead to disputes?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's try to find some common ground!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nIn his speech, Hank Josephson talks about how to <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">resolve</span> <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_1\">interpersonal</span> disputes.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}]}, {"type": "tips", "content": [{"tip_id": 0, "type": "text", "content": "To <span class=\"italic\">\u201cresolve\u201d</span> means to find a solution for something. Other words are <span class=\"italic\">to settle a dispute</span> or <span class=\"italic\">to solve a problem</span>."}, {"tip_id": 1, "type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">\u201cInterpersonal\u201d</span> means between two or more people."}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.\n"}]}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"type": "", "content": "to be a counselor."}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "used"}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 0, "text": "", "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "use"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 0, "text": "", "id": 2, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "will use"}], "selected": 0}]}, {"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"type": "", "content": "hear all sorts of people bla